{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/GettingStarted"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide is the shortest path from a wired Swidux app with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" registered to events landing in Mixpanel. It assumes you have already followed Swidux’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/Swidux\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" guide through Step 5 — that is, your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":" has an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"analytics"},{"type":"text","text":" slice, your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"type":"text","text":" routes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".analytics(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and you have an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsMapper"},{"type":"text","text":" declared."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Add-the-package","text":"Add the package","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Xcode:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" File > Add Package Dependencies, paste ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product to your target.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Package.swift:"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\", from: \"1.0.0\"),"]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".product(name: \"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\", package: \"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\"),"]},{"anchor":"Build-the-service-at-launch","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Build the service at launch"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" owns ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mixpanel.initialize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" internally — you do not need to ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Mixpanel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Construct the service with your token (and any Mixpanel knobs you care about) before configuring the store:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","import SwiftUI","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","    @State private var store: AppStore","","    init() {","        let analyticsService = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","            token: \"your-mixpanel-token\",","            optOutTrackingByDefault: true","        )","        _store = State(wrappedValue: AppStore.configured(analyticsService: analyticsService))","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup { ContentView().environment(store) }","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The initializer surfaces every Mixpanel knob the app would otherwise need to set on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"type":"text","text":" (EU "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"serverURL"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTrackingByDefault"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flushInterval"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instanceName"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"superProperties"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"useGzipCompression"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackAutomaticEvents"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"excludeProperties"},{"type":"text","text":") and is identical on every platform. Pick what you need; everything else has a sensible default. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the longer treatment."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Register-the-plugin-with-MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Register the plugin with `MixpanelAnalyticsService`"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass the service to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" factory:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Swidux","import SwiduxAnalytics","import SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","","extension Store where State == AppState, Action == AppAction {","    static func configured(analyticsService: some AnalyticsService) -> AppStore {","        let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","","        plugins.register(","            AnalyticsPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","                state: \\.analytics,","                action: AppAction.analytics,","                extractAction: { if case .analytics(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","                service: analyticsService,","                mapper: analyticsMapper,","                identity: analyticsIdentity","            )","        )","","        return Store(","            initialState: AppState(),","            reducer: AppReducer().reduce,","            plugins: plugins","        )","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That’s it — the plugin will route mapped events through the service, re-fire "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whenever the "},{"code":"(userID, userProperties)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pair derived from state changes, and flush on your call to "},{"code":"store.analyticsPlugin.flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"code":"scenePhase == .background","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Verify the wiring","anchor":"Verify-the-wiring","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Dispatch a screen view from your root view’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".onAppear","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and confirm the event arrives in Mixpanel’s Live View:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct ContentView: View {","    @Environment(AppStore.self) private var store","","    var body: some View {","        RootContent()","            .onAppear { store.send(.analytics(.screenView(\"Home\"))) }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService"},{"type":"text","text":" — EU residency, opt-out by default, multiple Mixpanel projects, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance"},{"type":"text","text":" escape hatch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest"},{"type":"text","text":" — Drive analytics state from previews and tests using "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — How ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cases map onto Mixpanel ","type":"text"},{"code":"Properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Add the package, build ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with your token, register the analytics plugin, and start dispatching events.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Getting Started with SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/gettingstarted"]}],"references":{"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics","title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel adapter for Swidux’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":". Owns the Mixpanel SDK on the app’s behalf — "},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService(token:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" calls "},{"code":"Mixpanel.initialize","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" internally so apps never need to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":". Ships a recording mock for previews and tests."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","role":"collection"},"https://heirloomlogic.github.io/Swidux/documentation/swidux/howtoaddanalytics":{"title":"Add Analytics","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Add Analytics","type":"text"}],"url":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/Swidux\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/Swidux\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/ValueTranslation":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/valuetranslation","title":"Value Translation","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsValue"},{"type":"text","text":" cases map onto Mixpanel’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelType"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Properties"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation","role":"article"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/HowToImplementService":{"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"How to Implement the Service","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtoimplementservice","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure "},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to match your privacy, residency, and batching needs — without ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Mixpanel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your app.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/HowToPreviewAndTest":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" from SwiftUI previews and Swift Testing suites without touching Mixpanel’s network."}],"role":"article","title":"How to Preview and Test","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtopreviewandtest","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mockmixpanelanalyticsservice","abstract":[{"text":"Recording ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"text":" for previews and Swift Testing suites.","type":"text"}],"title":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"}]}}}